  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Hz5su6uyRpob1Gv3UibqZdyoTMQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:27:55.284Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "First8 Conclusion describes itself as a Java and open-source applications shop, which means the open-source screen is passed by the firm's own self-description rather than by inference from a repository sweep. On the ethos axis that is about as strong a signal as a lead record can carry.\n\nThe cost falls entirely on technical affinity. The stack is Java rather than TypeScript, so an engagement would not land in a language the bench already works in daily. The assessment is explicit that this costs affinity but not ethos, and keeping the two scores separate is the point: a Java house that publishes its source is a materially different prospect from a TypeScript house that does not.\n\nThe record also marks this as a new row, so the lead entered the workbook late and has had less scrutiny than its neighbours. It sits at priority 2 as a Dutch Conclusion operating company.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- First8 Conclusion (NL \u00b7 opco)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> NEW ROW. Open source is in its self-description. Java rather than TypeScript, which costs it on technical affinity but not on ethos.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:27:55.284085Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:27:55.284090Z"
    }
  },
